WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
The surface of the Sun
is at about 5800 kelvin.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.850
Stars differ: some are
much hotter than the Sun,

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.370
others much cooler.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.080
All that reaches us from
a star is its light,

5
00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:15.390
spread across a continuous
range of wavelengths.

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.710
So how can that light alone tell
us how hot a star's surface is?

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.570
In this mission, you'll
meet the black body:

8
00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.180
it absorbs all the
radiation that falls on it,

9
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.680
and it is the best possible emitter.

10
00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:31.760
Then you'll find out why doubling a
body's temperature multiplies the power it

11
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.970
radiates by 16.

12
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.610
Your mission: find out how a star's
light reveals its surface temperature.
